figdown 0.1 block
# 0.1 retires THREE option keys language-wide. Unlike `color=` — which
# stayed registered on the thirteen directives that accepted it, so its
# message could be per-directive — these spellings left the language
# altogether: no directive accepts them, so the diagnostic fires WHEREVER the
# key appears (the `colw` → `width` precedent). A retired spelling must name
# its migration entry (PROCESS §5(d)); this case pins all three messages, and
# pins that the named diagnostic beats both the generic `unknown option` and
# the host directive's own "does not take" message.
#
#   w=   → width=    SVG, CSS, Graphviz DOT, mxGraph and D2 all spell the box
#   h=   → height=   attributes in full. `fill=`/`stroke=` were borrowed whole
#                    from SVG; abbreviating only the extent pair breaks the
#                    single-source vocabulary rule (`UNSAFE-DEFAULT-ELIMINATION`).
#   dir= → extend=   HTML's `dir` is TEXT WRITING DIRECTION. FigDown's meant
#                    "which way the band extends from its anchor" — the same
#                    spelling for a different meaning, an `UNSAFE-DEFAULT-ELIMINATION` defect.
#
# The INPUT below MUST be written in the RETIRED spellings — that is the whole
# point of the fixture. A bulk rename to the current spellings makes every
# line legal (or fail for an unrelated reason) and silently deletes the
# coverage; if you are running a migration over this directory, this file is
# the one to skip.
group g "G"
node a "A"
pin a w=120
pin a h=60
band "z" 15% in=g dir=up
# on a directive that never accepted the key, the retirement message is still
# the right answer — the OLD spelling is what does not belong there
node b "B" w=10
edge a -> b dir=down
